WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.733 --> 00:00:05.733
Our heroes are on their way to Anistar City,

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.266
where Ash hopes to win his seventh Kalos Gym Badge.

3
00:00:15.066 --> 00:00:18.133
- Ah. Is everybody all right?
- I'm OK.

4
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.500
- Yeah.
- Hey, what is this?

5
00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:24.633
Prepare for trouble, that's what this is!

6
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.966
And make it double, our team never misses!

7
00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:29.466
To protect the world from devastation!

8
00:00:29.533 --> 00:00:32.200
To unite all people within our nation!

9
00:00:32.266 --> 00:00:35.300
To denounce the evils of truth and love!

10
00:00:35.366 --> 00:00:38.700
Falling into a pit trap fits you like a glove!

11
00:00:38.766 --> 00:00:41.033
- Jessie!
- And James.

12
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.900
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light!

13
00:00:43.966 --> 00:00:47.033
Surrender now or prepare for a top-down fight.

14
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.466
Meowth, that's right!

15
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.766
♪ Na, na, na, boo, boo, we're free but not you! ♪

16
00:00:53.833 --> 00:00:56.766
- Team Rocket!
- Look, my hair's a mess.

17
00:00:56.833 --> 00:01:00.400
- Who cares, twerp?
- We're here for Pikachu.

18
00:01:00.466 --> 00:01:02.466
Give it up, if you know what's good for you.

19
00:01:02.533 --> 00:01:06.200
Not a chance. Pikachu, use Thunderbolt.

20
00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:08.833
- Pikachu!
- Back atcha, dolt!

21
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.800
This net will keep unwanted zaps from zappin'.

22
00:01:12.866 --> 00:01:15.933
Bunnelby, Mud Shot, let's go.

23
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Bunnelby!

24
00:01:18.066 --> 00:01:20.600
-'Kay, Pikachu, Thunderbolt, now!

25
00:01:20.666 --> 00:01:23.833
Pikachu!

26
00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:26.900
I want more screen time!

27
00:01:26.966 --> 00:01:29.666
We're blasting off again!

28
00:01:31.433 --> 00:01:33.933
- And stay away!
- Hey!

29
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.266
-Pika!

30
00:01:35.333 --> 00:01:38.933
-Pika!

31
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.800
♪ You're just a kid on a quest ♪

32
00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:42.566
♪ To be the best of the best ♪

33
00:01:42.633 --> 00:01:46.000
♪ Someday you're destined for power and glory ♪

34
00:01:46.066 --> 00:01:47.466
♪ You know you're up to the test ♪

35
00:01:47.533 --> 00:01:51.300
♪ There's only one way to tell this story ♪

36
00:01:51.366 --> 00:01:54.566
♪ Be a hero! Be a hero! ♪

37
00:01:54.633 --> 00:01:58.000
♪ All the power is at your command ♪

38
00:01:58.066 --> 00:02:02.033
♪ Face your fears and show you're a hero ♪

39
00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:06.733
♪ The future of the world is in your hand! ♪

40
00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.000
♪ Pokémon! ♪

41
00:02:12.933 --> 00:02:16.066
A Trip Down Memory Train!

42
00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:25.300
- Ah, I hit my head.
- Pika.

43
00:02:25.366 --> 00:02:26.800
Hey, guys, we all here?

44
00:02:26.866 --> 00:02:29.833
- Uh-huh.
- All of us.

45
00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:33.833
- Bunnelby.
- Big booms like that are a lot of fun.

46
00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.033
Denne-ne.

47
00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:38.766
- What a fall.
- It's a long way down here.

48
00:02:38.833 --> 00:02:41.766
Pika, Pikachu.

49
00:02:41.833 --> 00:02:44.766
It looks like an abandoned mine.

50
00:02:44.833 --> 00:02:47.533
- Pika, pika!
- What is it, Pikachu?

51
00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.900
- Of course. Let's follow these tracks.
- Then we can get out.

52
00:02:50.966 --> 00:02:51.800
That's right.

53
00:02:51.866 --> 00:02:55.066
Hm. OK. Let's get out of here.

54
00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:57.233
Pikachu!

55
00:03:00.766 --> 00:03:03.966
Hey, Clemont? I think this happened to us once before.

56
00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:06.633
- Yeah? Bonnie, you think so?
- Of course.

57
00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.566
When we first met Bunnelby.

58
00:03:08.633 --> 00:03:10.633
- Oh, right.
- Yeah?

59
00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:13.466
- So, what happened, you guys?
- Tell us about it.

60
00:03:13.533 --> 00:03:14.566
Pikachu!

61
00:03:14.633 --> 00:03:18.800
- You sure you really wanna know?
- They asked you, so tell them.

62
00:03:18.866 --> 00:03:21.300
- All right, then, if you insist.
- Awesome.

63
00:03:22.266 --> 00:03:26.033
Let's see. It was after Clembot threw me out of the Lumiose Gym.

64
00:03:27.033 --> 00:03:32.400
I was spending all my time trying to figure out how I could get back inside.

65
00:03:32.466 --> 00:03:35.666
Ah! What am I going to do?

66
00:03:35.733 --> 00:03:40.300
Uh? So hungry. I need food. I can't even think straight.

67
00:03:40.366 --> 00:03:41.766
- Clemont?
- Huh?

68
00:03:41.833 --> 00:03:44.133
Sorry.

69
00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.533
This is all I could find in the house.

70
00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.966
Wow, how nice of you.

71
00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:55.700
- Hey, you! Stop!
- I want to eat that! Give it back!

72
00:03:55.766 --> 00:03:57.933
- Pika?
- Bunnelby really did that?

73
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.200
I can't imagine Bunnelby doing that kind of thing now.

74
00:04:01.266 --> 00:04:03.766
- Pikachu.
- Bunnelby.

75
00:04:03.833 --> 00:04:07.766
Anyway, that's how Bunnelby and I first met.

76
00:04:10.466 --> 00:04:13.466
- Where's that Bunnelby?
- It's gone.

77
00:04:13.533 --> 00:04:15.900
Huh? Over there!

78
00:04:15.966 --> 00:04:18.399
Stop! You won't get away!

79
00:04:18.466 --> 00:04:21.700
Oops. Uh-oh.

80
00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:30.200
- Bonnie, are you OK?
- I think so.

81
00:04:31.233 --> 00:04:35.600
- Huh? Clemont, what's this?
- It looks to me like a subway tunnel.

82
00:04:35.666 --> 00:04:39.166
Aah! I'm scared! What if a train comes?

83
00:04:39.233 --> 00:04:43.833
We'll be fine. I'm pretty sure this subway line isn't in use any more.

84
00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:46.666
That's good. Bunnelby! Where'd it go?

85
00:04:46.733 --> 00:04:49.333
Who knows? Forget it.

86
00:04:50.533 --> 00:04:53.066
Let's just get out.

87
00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:55.900
Great, I knew I had a subway map in here.

88
00:04:55.966 --> 00:05:01.200
That's it. Calculating from the point where we fell, let's head west.

89
00:05:01.266 --> 00:05:04.100
- That'll get us out.
- Big brother does it again.

90
00:05:11.466 --> 00:05:13.633
Clemont, it's a station!

91
00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.200
I know it's scheduled to be demolished,

92
00:05:16.266 --> 00:05:19.833
but the construction is remarkably well preserved.

93
00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:25.000
Grab on. Up you go!

94
00:05:25.066 --> 00:05:27.500
-Ah, all right.

95
00:05:27.566 --> 00:05:30.233
Now we just need to go through the exit.

96
00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.666
By, by. Bunnelby.

97
00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.833
By! Bunn, bunn, bunn.

98
00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:49.400
So that's why Bunnelby took it.

99
00:05:49.466 --> 00:05:52.833
- Bunnelby's so sweet.
- Yeah.

100
00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:56.233
I guess they're all helping each other out. That's nice.

101
00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.333
Why do you think they live down here?

102
00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.933
I'd say it keeps them out of the rain.

103
00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:04.000
And they can stay warm, no matter what it's like outside.

104
00:06:04.066 --> 00:06:05.266
Uh, huh.

105
00:06:05.333 --> 00:06:07.500
See, for city-dwelling Pokémon,

106
00:06:07.566 --> 00:06:11.333
finding a secure and cosy place to live is the most important thing.

107
00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:14.700
So for Bunnelby and the rest of them, this is like their home.

108
00:06:14.766 --> 00:06:15.866
Diggersby.

109
00:06:15.933 --> 00:06:18.033
Skitty!

110
00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:20.533
- Diggersby!
- Bunnelby!

111
00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:24.033
- Digg!
- Bunn! By!

112
00:06:27.233 --> 00:06:28.666
Hey, what's going on?

113
00:06:28.733 --> 00:06:31.466
I think that Diggersby is trying to kick everyone out

114
00:06:31.533 --> 00:06:33.166
and take the train for its own.

115
00:06:33.233 --> 00:06:36.733
Hey, that's not nice. You've got to help them, please?

116
00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:39.633
- But how?
- By! Mm.

117
00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:43.166
- Bunnelby!
- Diggersby!

118
00:06:44.233 --> 00:06:46.400
- Bunn.
- Digg!

119
00:06:46.466 --> 00:06:48.300
Bunnelby!

120
00:06:50.166 --> 00:06:51.833
Bunn!

121
00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:53.933
- No.
- That Diggersby is too strong.

122
00:06:54.066 --> 00:06:56.233
By!

123
00:06:57.166 --> 00:07:00.666
Bunnelby! By! By! By! By!

124
00:07:00.733 --> 00:07:02.166
- Digg!
- Bunn.

125
00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:04.900
Huh?

126
00:07:05.733 --> 00:07:07.566
- Digg...
- By!

127
00:07:07.633 --> 00:07:10.200
- Bunn!
- By!

128
00:07:10.266 --> 00:07:11.866
By!

129
00:07:12.866 --> 00:07:14.633
By! By! Bunn! Bunn! Bunn!

130
00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.766
Diggersby!

131
00:07:16.833 --> 00:07:18.000
Bunn!

132
00:07:18.066 --> 00:07:20.166
-Please, Clemont!

133
00:07:20.233 --> 00:07:22.333
- You've got to help.
- But how?

134
00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:23.800
My Pokémon are at the gym.

135
00:07:23.866 --> 00:07:26.366
- Bunn?
- Clemont!

136
00:07:26.433 --> 00:07:28.666
Go, Aipom Arm!

137
00:07:30.066 --> 00:07:32.433
-That's my big brother.

138
00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:34.600
- You're all right now.
- Bunn.

139
00:07:34.666 --> 00:07:36.333
Diggersby.

140
00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:39.466
Digg!

141
00:07:40.333 --> 00:07:42.466
Everybody, retreat!

142
00:07:44.266 --> 00:07:47.100
- Horrible.
- So, what happened next?

143
00:07:47.166 --> 00:07:49.933
- Pika, pika!
- Bunnelby!

144
00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:52.766
- Relax. Just tell them.
- Denne, denne!

145
00:07:52.833 --> 00:07:56.266
After that, Bonnie said...

146
00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:02.066
- Del.
- Skitty.

147
00:08:02.133 --> 00:08:06.000
- Hey, Clemont, Bunnelby needs first aid.
- I know.

148
00:08:06.066 --> 00:08:09.166
But my area of expertise is Electric types.

149
00:08:09.233 --> 00:08:13.100
- You can do anything.
- Hm.

150
00:08:13.166 --> 00:08:14.233
I'll give it a try.

151
00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.700
-Patrat, rat!

152
00:08:17.766 --> 00:08:20.966
Don't be afraid. I'm just gonna try to help Bunnelby.

153
00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:23.733
See, we're friends with all of you. Really.

154
00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:27.233
- Zigzagoon.
- Patrat.

155
00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:28.700
Delcatty.

156
00:08:28.766 --> 00:08:30.300
Mm-hm.

157
00:08:35.333 --> 00:08:37.200
Miaow.

158
00:08:40.366 --> 00:08:42.333
Bunn.

159
00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:46.333
- There, I'm all done.
- Bunn! By! Bunnelby, by, by!

160
00:08:47.466 --> 00:08:49.833
- Not again.
- Please don't.

161
00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:52.633
Diggersby's just too strong for you to fight.

162
00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:56.366
By? Bunn...

163
00:08:57.266 --> 00:09:00.800
- However, that doesn't mean you can't win.
- By?

164
00:09:00.866 --> 00:09:05.200
Believe it or not, my brother is the Lumiose City Gym Leader.

165
00:09:05.266 --> 00:09:08.166
-He knows all about Pokémon battles.

166
00:09:08.233 --> 00:09:09.566
Now, listen to me.

167
00:09:09.633 --> 00:09:12.733
When you're up against someone big like Diggersby,

168
00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:15.066
strategic battling is better than brute force.

169
00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:20.400
You can use Dig or Double Team to dodge your opponents.

170
00:09:20.466 --> 00:09:22.866
If possible, use your opponent's power!

171
00:09:22.933 --> 00:09:24.866
Bunnelby?

172
00:09:26.033 --> 00:09:28.800
Don't get it, huh? OK.

173
00:09:28.866 --> 00:09:32.500
- Then we'll just act it out!
- Act it out?

174
00:09:34.766 --> 00:09:38.733
- Now, I'll be Diggersby.
- And I'll be Bunnelby.

175
00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:41.866
- By?
- First, I'll use Hammer Arm.

176
00:09:41.933 --> 00:09:45.866
-And I'll dodge using Dig. Brrr!

177
00:09:45.933 --> 00:09:48.766
Bunnelby dodged it! Oh!

178
00:09:48.833 --> 00:09:52.433
- Ugh. Ow.
- Huh, like that.

179
00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:53.466
Bunnel!

180
00:09:53.533 --> 00:09:57.466
Now what if I do this? Super Fang! Aaah!

181
00:09:57.533 --> 00:09:59.800
- Use Double Team!
- Aaaaah!

182
00:09:59.866 --> 00:10:02.466
I'll find the real Bunnelby with Double Kick!

183
00:10:02.533 --> 00:10:04.333
- Awww!
- Hmph!

184
00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:07.033
All right, you'll use your long ears to defend.

185
00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:09.233
Bunnelby. Bunn.

186
00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:11.366
Bunnelby!

187
00:10:11.433 --> 00:10:12.733
-Yippee.

188
00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:16.166
Your ears should be a good defence against a lot of things.

189
00:10:16.233 --> 00:10:18.133
Huh? Right.

190
00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:20.700
If you use your ears, you'll win for sure.

191
00:10:22.566 --> 00:10:23.933
Bunnelby!

192
00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:27.133
Who's that Pokémon?

193
00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.766
It's Trubbish!

194
00:10:33.833 --> 00:10:36.933
Trubbish!

195
00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:38.866
OK, then what happened?

196
00:10:38.933 --> 00:10:40.166
Pika, pika!

197
00:10:40.233 --> 00:10:44.033
I did some special training with Bunnelby so they could get their homes back.

198
00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:46.133
And then we went to challenge Diggersby, right?

199
00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:49.133
Bunnelby.

200
00:10:53.933 --> 00:10:55.766
You can do it, Bunnelby.

201
00:10:55.833 --> 00:10:58.233
- Bunnelby!
- Diggersby!

202
00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:01.733
It's starting with Hammer Arm. It's just like we trained for.

203
00:11:01.866 --> 00:11:04.133
- By, by!
- Bunn! Brrr!

204
00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:09.600
- Way to go!
- Diggersby! Oof!

205
00:11:10.366 --> 00:11:14.300
- That was a great combination!
- Diggersby!

206
00:11:14.366 --> 00:11:17.333
By! Brrrr!

207
00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:21.066
Diggersby!

208
00:11:21.133 --> 00:11:23.600
By! Bunn.

209
00:11:23.666 --> 00:11:26.733
All of our training is working.

210
00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:29.466
Diggersby!

211
00:11:29.533 --> 00:11:32.600
- By! By! Bunn! Bunn!
- Diggersby!

212
00:11:32.666 --> 00:11:35.333
Bunnelby!

213
00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:38.000
- Bunn!
- Diggersby...

214
00:11:38.066 --> 00:11:42.466
- All right!
- Diggersby!

215
00:11:42.533 --> 00:11:43.800
Bunn!

216
00:11:43.866 --> 00:11:47.300
- Yippee, yippee!
- Look at the way Bunnelby blocked.

217
00:11:47.366 --> 00:11:50.933
- By, bunn!
- Digger...

218
00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:52.633
Bunnel?

219
00:11:53.566 --> 00:11:56.366
By? Bunn. By, by, by.

220
00:11:58.233 --> 00:12:00.433
Digg.

221
00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:01.933
Bunnelby?

222
00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.600
- Bunnelby wants to make up.
- By...

223
00:12:05.733 --> 00:12:07.866
Digg.

224
00:12:07.933 --> 00:12:08.933
By.

225
00:12:10.866 --> 00:12:15.300
Digg. By!

226
00:12:16.766 --> 00:12:18.066
- Bunnel.
- Huh?

227
00:12:18.133 --> 00:12:20.533
Hey, you did the best you could, Bunnelby.

228
00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:24.200
- You offered to make peace. You tried.
- Bunnelby.

229
00:12:24.266 --> 00:12:27.200
Make peace. You know what?

230
00:12:27.266 --> 00:12:30.266
You and Bunnelby are a really good team.

231
00:12:30.333 --> 00:12:31.466
- Huh?
- Bunn?

232
00:12:34.033 --> 00:12:36.466
Bunn, Bunnelby!

233
00:12:40.533 --> 00:12:43.800
- What was that?
- Uh? Oh, no!

234
00:12:43.866 --> 00:12:47.900
They started demolishing the station.

235
00:12:47.966 --> 00:12:51.300
- We're in danger down here.
- Everyone, run.

236
00:12:51.366 --> 00:12:53.300
- Bunnel.
- Of course.

237
00:12:53.366 --> 00:12:55.733
None of you wanna leave here, do you?

238
00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:57.400
But why?

239
00:12:57.466 --> 00:13:01.466
Because this is their home!

240
00:13:04.533 --> 00:13:08.800
I know. How about we move their train to a safe place?

241
00:13:10.366 --> 00:13:14.333
- There. I know the perfect location.
- You do?

242
00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:18.766
All right. Let's get this train moving and find you a new home.

243
00:13:18.833 --> 00:13:20.300
- Bunn.
- Think you can do that?

244
00:13:20.366 --> 00:13:23.800
Hah. The future is now, thanks to science.

245
00:13:23.866 --> 00:13:26.333
Clemontic Gear, on.

246
00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:30.900
I thought that we'd encounter a situation precisely like this one.

247
00:13:30.966 --> 00:13:33.933
I call this my Running Generator. Hah!

248
00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:37.933
It generates electricity as you run on top of the conveyor belt.

249
00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:40.400
But how's that gonna help?

250
00:13:40.466 --> 00:13:42.800
It lets us get the train moving.

251
00:13:42.866 --> 00:13:46.733
First off, I connect the cord. Aah!

252
00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:49.066
- Look, in the middle of the track!
- Ah.

253
00:13:49.133 --> 00:13:53.066
Now what? Even with enough power, we can't get past that rock.

254
00:13:56.466 --> 00:14:01.466
-Diggersby! By!

255
00:14:02.466 --> 00:14:05.500
- Diggersby.
- That was so nice!

256
00:14:05.566 --> 00:14:08.000
Diggersby!

257
00:14:09.166 --> 00:14:13.966
Clemont, do you think maybe Diggersby wants to come along with everybody else?

258
00:14:14.033 --> 00:14:15.866
- Mm-hm.
- Bunn!

259
00:14:15.933 --> 00:14:18.100
Digg?

260
00:14:18.166 --> 00:14:20.600
Bunnelby.

261
00:14:22.266 --> 00:14:24.100
Mm.

262
00:14:24.166 --> 00:14:26.600
Diggersby!

263
00:14:26.666 --> 00:14:28.366
Bunnelby!

264
00:14:29.233 --> 00:14:32.333
Wow, this time they really did make up.

265
00:14:33.566 --> 00:14:35.500
Oh, no! We've gotta hurry!

266
00:14:35.566 --> 00:14:39.266
Everyone, we're going to need your help. I'll drive the train.

267
00:14:39.333 --> 00:14:41.066
Bunnelby!

268
00:14:43.066 --> 00:14:44.266
Diggersby.

269
00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:49.566
- Now, let's get outta here.
- All set!

270
00:14:58.333 --> 00:15:00.100
- We're on.
- Diggersby. Diggersby!

271
00:15:01.433 --> 00:15:03.700
Full power. Now!

272
00:15:03.766 --> 00:15:07.066
-It worked!

273
00:15:09.766 --> 00:15:11.800
Way to go! We're moving!

274
00:15:17.866 --> 00:15:23.100
Let's see. It looks like we need to bear right at the next junction.

275
00:15:23.166 --> 00:15:24.900
But where's the switch?

276
00:15:24.966 --> 00:15:26.600
Oh, no, it's pointed left!

277
00:15:26.666 --> 00:15:29.600
-What'll we do?

278
00:15:29.666 --> 00:15:31.366
- By!
- Bunnelby!

279
00:15:31.433 --> 00:15:33.200
Bunnelby!

280
00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:38.966
Bunnelby, you switched the tracks. Thanks a lot.

281
00:15:39.033 --> 00:15:40.533
Bunn!

282
00:15:42.566 --> 00:15:46.133
Ah, are we there yet, Clemont? I'm so tired.

283
00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:49.066
Just a little bit more. Keep going.

284
00:15:49.133 --> 00:15:54.000
Huh? Hey, look! I can see the exit.

285
00:15:57.166 --> 00:15:59.033
- Yay!

286
00:16:06.666 --> 00:16:08.033
We made it!

287
00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:11.033
By!

288
00:16:13.633 --> 00:16:17.566
There are no plans to reopen this or do any further construction.

289
00:16:18.733 --> 00:16:22.700
You've got the train you love and plenty to eat growing all around you,

290
00:16:22.766 --> 00:16:27.700
- so you certainly won't go hungry.
- It's really a great place.

291
00:16:27.766 --> 00:16:30.200
Bunnel!

292
00:16:32.733 --> 00:16:33.733
Bunn?

293
00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:43.200
Hey, maybe it's time to go back.

294
00:16:43.266 --> 00:16:49.000
- Huh? You're right. OK. We're going now.
- Bunn.

295
00:16:49.066 --> 00:16:52.800
Stay safe, everybody.

296
00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:56.966
'Kay, bye-bye!

297
00:17:06.166 --> 00:17:08.366
Bunnelby.

298
00:17:08.433 --> 00:17:10.166
- Del.
- Huh?

299
00:17:10.233 --> 00:17:12.266
Delcatty.

300
00:17:12.333 --> 00:17:14.666
Bunn, Bunnelby.

301
00:17:17.966 --> 00:17:21.466
- Zig. Zigzagoon.
- Digg.

302
00:17:22.133 --> 00:17:26.700
- Diggersby! By, by!
- Delcatty, del.

303
00:17:26.766 --> 00:17:28.466
Diggersby!

304
00:17:31.033 --> 00:17:32.700
Kitty!

305
00:17:32.766 --> 00:17:35.700
- Patrat!
- Tru, tru, tru.

306
00:17:39.633 --> 00:17:41.766
Bunn, Bunnelby!

307
00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:45.200
Bunnelby!

308
00:17:46.333 --> 00:17:50.700
Bunn, bunn, bunn, bunn!

309
00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:58.633
- They looked really happy, didn't they?
- Mm-hm.

310
00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:00.833
Bunnelby!

311
00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.100
-It's Bunnelby.

312
00:18:03.166 --> 00:18:05.433
- What is it?
- Bunn, Bunnelby!

313
00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:07.966
- Hey, what do you mean?
- That's right.

314
00:18:08.033 --> 00:18:10.900
Bunnelby wants to come along with you real badly.

315
00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:17.633
Hm?

316
00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:20.733
Wow, Bunnelby, will you really come back with me?

317
00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:24.333
Bunn, bunn. By!

318
00:18:26.566 --> 00:18:27.833
There you have it.

319
00:18:27.900 --> 00:18:31.000
That's how Bunnelby and I became the team we are now.

320
00:18:31.066 --> 00:18:32.500
Bunnel.

321
00:18:32.566 --> 00:18:34.366
What a great story!

322
00:18:34.433 --> 00:18:36.800
So does that mean Bunnelby's the first Pokémon

323
00:18:36.866 --> 00:18:39.666
- you've had who isn't an Electric type?
- Pikachu.

324
00:18:39.733 --> 00:18:42.466
It sure is. And thanks to Bunnelby's help,

325
00:18:42.533 --> 00:18:45.166
I was able to take my gym back from Clembot.

326
00:18:45.233 --> 00:18:47.866
- Yeah, you sure did.
- Bunn!

327
00:18:47.933 --> 00:18:50.700
-Pika?

328
00:18:50.766 --> 00:18:54.000
- It's a dead end!
- Uh, all right.

329
00:18:54.066 --> 00:18:56.633
- Bunnelby, use Dig!
- By!

330
00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:58.700
Bunn...

331
00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:03.400
-Pika!

332
00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:08.433
We're finally out!

333
00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:11.766
Fresh air.

334
00:19:11.833 --> 00:19:14.533
You didn't tell them the rest of the story, you know.

335
00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:15.600
Huh?

336
00:19:15.666 --> 00:19:17.433
- I think they've heard enough.
- What, what?

337
00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:20.266
- Come on. Tell us!
- Pika, pika!

338
00:19:20.333 --> 00:19:21.333
Bunn.

339
00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:24.100
Well, you see...

340
00:19:28.633 --> 00:19:30.566
Here goes. Hm!

341
00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:44.166
Come out, Bunnelby.

342
00:19:46.100 --> 00:19:47.433
Bunn, Bunnelby.

343
00:19:49.233 --> 00:19:53.100
After we parted ways, I was so glad you came back.

344
00:19:53.166 --> 00:19:56.400
- You've made me so happy.
- By?

345
00:19:56.466 --> 00:19:59.733
I'll never be able to thank you enough, Bunnelby!

346
00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:02.333
We'll be together forever and ever!

347
00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:07.100
-Bunn! Bunn.

348
00:20:07.633 --> 00:20:09.200
That's the real ending.

349
00:20:09.266 --> 00:20:11.100
None of that's the truth!

350
00:20:11.166 --> 00:20:14.300
There wasn't any crying at all. Bonnie's exaggerating.

351
00:20:14.366 --> 00:20:15.500
OK.

352
00:20:15.566 --> 00:20:17.400
Hey, Clemont, nothin' wrong with crying.

353
00:20:17.466 --> 00:20:19.866
Pikachu.

354
00:20:19.933 --> 00:20:21.066
That's right.

355
00:20:21.133 --> 00:20:23.700
Oh, then you were crying!

356
00:20:23.766 --> 00:20:26.233
- Huh?
- By! Bunnelby!

357
00:20:27.366 --> 00:20:32.200
- Bunnelby, you're simply the best.
- Bunn, Bunnelby.

358
00:20:33.266 --> 00:20:35.500
A heartwarming tale of times past

359
00:20:35.566 --> 00:20:38.966
led Clemont and Bunnelby to reaffirm their bonds of friendship.

360
00:20:39.033 --> 00:20:41.766
Now, with all their friendships stronger than ever,

361
00:20:41.833 --> 00:20:45.900
our heroes' journey to Anistar City continues.
